# This context serves both images built from the repository: the dev container
# (.devcontainer/Dockerfile) and the image the root Dockerfile builds. That
# Dockerfile's COPY list is the wheel build's whole input set - pyproject.toml,
# README.md, LICENSE and src/ - and the exclusions below keep the directories
# and artifacts no build can need out of the context; the remaining tracked
# files still travel with it. The dev container needs
# .devcontainer/entrypoint.sh, so nothing under .devcontainer is excluded.
.git
.github
.venv
# The **/ prefix matches caches beside the code, not only at the repo root.
**/__pycache__
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.env
dist
tests
docs
# The paper source: no build reads it.
paper
